  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 丙\ntitle: third rank; third heavenly stem\njlpt: 1\ntags: [jlpt-n1, grade-8, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 5\nradical: 一\nradicalNumber: 1\nonyomi: [ヘイ]\nkunyomi: [ひのえ]\nquizOnyomi: [ヘイ]\nquizKunyomi: [ひのえ]\ndistractors: [内, 肉, 病]\n---\n\n# 丙 — third rank; third heavenly stem\n\n**Strokes:** 5 · **Key (radical):** 一 (no. 1) · **JLPT:** N1 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n丙 names the third position in the label sequence 甲・乙・丙 (こう・おつ・へい),\ncomparable to A, B, C. It also names the third of the ten **heavenly stems**:\ntraditional calendar labels, not the twelve animal signs. This stem is associated\nwith fire in the traditional classification.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** picture a separate top [一](一.md) bar\nabove an [内](内.md)-like shape. The inner descending stroke reaches up to that\ntop bar. Use the extra bar to distinguish 丙 from 内.\nHistorical explanations differ; no settled origin is asserted here.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ヘイ | on | [丙](../words/丙.md) へい — third rank; class C |\n| ひのえ | kun | [丙午](../words/丙午.md) ひのえうま — Fire Horse, a calendar term combining 丙 ひのえ with 午 うま |\n\nUse へい for the rank/class label. The native calendar name is ひのえ.\nThe stem can also be called へい; 丙午 has the documented alternate reading\nへいご. That alternate does not replace the ひのえうま model in the kun row.\n\n## Common words\n\nThese are label and calendar uses, not ordinary counting vocabulary.\n\n- [丙](../words/丙.md) へい — the third rank or class in a 甲・乙・丙 sequence\n- [丙午](../words/丙午.md) ひのえうま — Fire Horse, term 43 of the sixty-term calendar cycle\n\n## Notes\n\n- **Not the numeral three:** [三](三.md) さん counts a quantity. 丙 is a\n  particular label; do not substitute it for 三 in ordinary counting.\n- **Ten, twelve, sixty:** 十干 (じっかん) are the ten stems, and 十二支\n  (じゅうにし) are the twelve branches associated with animals.\n  Pairing the two sequences in order produces a cycle of sixty terms.\n  丙 is a stem; [午](午.md) うま is the Horse branch.\n- **Look-alikes:** [内](内.md) lacks the separate top bar; [肉](肉.md)\n  has two stacked inner person-like marks instead. [病](病.md) has additional\n  enclosing sickness-radical strokes around the 丙-shaped part. These are\n  modern-shape comparisons, not claims about historical formation.\n\nUsage: [Kanjipedia, 丙](https://www.kanjipedia.jp/kanji/0006192100) and\n[丙午](https://www.kanjipedia.jp/kotoba/0006192700).\nDictionary data: [KANJIDIC2 and JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/)\n(J. W. Breen / EDRDG; [CC BY-SA 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)).\n",
